      "answerKeyRef": null,
      "explanation": "Answer B: Liver failure. Low BUN can occur with reduced hepatic urea synthesis (e.g. severe liver dysfunction); dehydration, obstruction and prerenal azotemia more often raise BUN. Reference: https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/bun-blood-urea-nitrogen/. Verified worked solution, unofficial. Original printed wording and option order reviewed; no matching examiner key is asserted.",
